SUMMARY:Chris Smither
LOCATION:Iron Horse\, 18 Center St\, Northampton\, MA 01060
DESCRIPTION:Born in Miami\, during World War II\, Chris Smither grew up in 
 New Orleans where he first started playing music as a child. The son of a 
 Tulane University professor\, he was taught the rudiments of instrumentati
 on by his uncle on his mother’s ukulele. “Uncle Howard\,” Smither sa
 ys\, “showed me that if you knew three chords\, you could play a lot of 
 the songs you heard on the radio. And if you knew four chords\, you could 
 pretty much rule the world.” With that bit of knowledge under his belt\,
  he was hooked. “I’d loved acoustic music – specifically the blues 
 – ever since I first heard Lightnin’ Hopkins’ Blues In My Bottle alb
 um. I couldn’t believe the sound Hopkins got. At first I thought it was 
 two guys playing guitar. My style\, to a degree\, came out of trying to im
 itate that sound I heard.”\nhttps://theparlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.co
 m/ticket/#/instances/a0FV500000KQ3oRMAT\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https:
 //pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://theparlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/instances/a0FV50
 0000KQ3oRMAT
END:VEVENT
